Third-party code and data in this branch
========================================

The JM2D code in this repository is released under the MIT License (LICENSE). Parts of it derive from the projects
below, which keep their own copyright and license. Licenses were checked on GitHub on 2026-10-15.

diffuser/  (package name kept so that the released checkpoint pickles load)
  * DPCC, Ralf Römer et al., "Diffusion Predictive Control with Constraints" (L4DC 2025),
    https://github.com/ralfroemer99/dpcc
    The D3IL code base was forked from DPCC in Oct-Dec 2024; the fork carried NO LICENSE file.
    Upstream has since added an MIT License ("Copyright (c) 2025 Learning Systems and Robotics Lab (LSY)", commit
    "Add license", 2026-08-15).
    OPEN ITEM FOR THE AUTHORS: confirm with the DPCC authors that the MIT license covers the forked code (or obtain
    permission), and copy their copyright notice here before the public release.
    Files: diffuser/{datasets,models,sampling,utils}/* except the JM2D additions listed below. The `dpcc` planner runs
    the DPCC sampling loop of that code base (diffuser/models/dpcc_diffusion.py, per-step projection).
  * Diffuser, Michael Janner et al., https://github.com/jannerm/diffuser, MIT License
    (its LICENSE: "Copyright (c) 2020 Phil Wang"). DPCC builds on Diffuser's temporal U-Net, diffusion model and
    training utilities (diffuser/models/{helpers,unet1d_temporal_cond,diffusion}.py, diffuser/utils/*,
    diffuser/datasets/*).
  * Decision Diffuser, Anurag Ajay et al., https://github.com/anuragajay/decision-diffuser: the return-conditioned
    U-Net / classifier-free guidance options (`returns_condition`, `condition_guidance_w`, `calc_energy`,
    `GaussianInvDynDiffusion` hooks) in the files above appear to follow its code. That repository shows no license on
    GitHub. OPEN ITEM: confirm the provenance / attribution of these parts.

diffuser/models/invariance.py
  SafeDiffuser invariance (RoS / ReS / TVS) modules, "largely adapted from" https://github.com/Weixy21/SafeDiffuser
  (Wei Xiao et al.), MIT License ("Copyright (c) 2025 Wei Xiao").

diffuser/models/diffusion.py  (MPD guidance in GaussianDiffusion.p_mean_variance)
  Cost-gradient guidance in the style of Motion Planning Diffusion (Carvalho et al.), implemented for this code base
  (no code copied).

third_party/d3il.patch
  Patch to D3IL, https://github.com/ALRhub/d3il, MIT License ("Copyright (c) 2024 Autonomous Learning Robots Lab @
  KIT"): imports rewritten to the `d3il.environments...` package path and
  `ObstacleAvoidanceEnv.start(override_init_pos=None)`. The D3IL code and the Avoiding demonstrations are not
  redistributed here (README: clone + patch + data download).

Python dependencies (installed, not vendored), e.g. torch (BSD-3), diffusers (Apache-2.0), qpth (Apache-2.0),
cvxpy (Apache-2.0), scipy / numpy (BSD-3), mujoco (Apache-2.0), pinocchio (BSD-2), keep their own licenses.

JM2D additions (this work, MIT): diffuser/models/jm2d.py, the JM2D branch of diffuser/models/dpcc_diffusion.py,
diffuser/sampling/policies.py (DPCCPolicy use_jm2d), jm2d_d3il/, configs/, scripts/, tests/, paper/.
